---
import StoryLayout from '../../layouts/StoryLayout.astro';
import ProjectFigure from '../../components/ProjectFigure.astro';
import MarioUniversalisInfographic from '../../components/MarioUniversalisInfographic.astro';
import { guessr, universalis, storyImages } from '../../data/projects';
import { workPath } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { en as copy } from '../../i18n/en';
const locale = 'en';
---
<StoryLayout locale={locale} copy={copy} slug={universalis.slug} name={universalis.name} title="Mario Universalis: where I learned the web" description="Since 2007, a Mario fansite has been my testing ground for PHP, GraphQL, Gatsby, guides, SEO, bots and games." context={'Since ' + universalis.created}>

  <Fragment slot="introduction"><p>I launched <strong>Mario Universalis</strong> in high school, in {universalis.created}. My goal was to share my passion for the world of <em>Super Mario</em>. It was an opportunity to discover HTML and CSS through <em>Le Site du Zéro</em>. Almost twenty years later, <strong>Mario Universalis</strong> has grown into a small ecosystem, and I am still learning by building things around it.</p></Fragment>
  <MarioUniversalisInfographic locale={locale} caption="An ecosystem that has evolved alongside my career and continues to regularly give rise to new projects." />
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="learning">
    <h2 id="learning">Learning with something to build.</h2>
    <div class="prose"><p><strong>Mario Universalis</strong> has always been my technical testing ground. After HTML and CSS, it gave me a real project through which to learn PHP/MySQL and then JavaScript, with several thousand visitors: in its early days, it was one of the first <em>Super Mario</em> fansites!</p><p>Today, the original PHP and JavaScript website lives alongside more modern projects built with React, Gatsby, GraphQL, and other technologies. Some parts are very old; others are less than a year old. The projects around <strong>Mario Universalis</strong> evolve alongside me.</p></div>
  </section>
  <header class="projects-heading"><h2>A closer look at a few Mario Universalis projects.</h2></header>
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="wonder">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
      <h3 id="wonder">Complete Super Mario Bros. Wonder walkthrough.</h3>
      <p>A project dedicated to SEO.</p>
      <a class="project-direct-link" href={universalis.wonderUrl}>View project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="prose"><p>I set myself the slightly crazy challenge of writing a complete walkthrough for <strong>Super Mario Bros. Wonder</strong>. Alongside sharing a free guide (with no ads!) that could help many players, I paid particular attention to its SEO. If you search for a French-language guide to the game, there is a good chance it will appear among the top five results!</p></div>
  </section>
  <ProjectFigure image={storyImages.wonder} alt="A page from the Super Mario Bros. Wonder walkthrough on Mario Universalis." pending={copy.labels.figurePending}>
    <Fragment slot="caption">Special attention was paid to the SEO of the <strong>Super Mario Bros. Wonder</strong> walkthrough: <em>Google Search Console</em> reports more than <strong>1 million impressions</strong> and <strong>123,000 organic clicks</strong>, with an <strong>average CTR of 11.9%</strong> and an <strong>average position of 4.4</strong> over a period of just over a year following the guide's publication.</Fragment>
  </ProjectFigure>
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="guessr">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
      <h3 id="guessr">Mario Kart World Guessr.</h3>
      <p>A project played around the world.</p>
      <a class="project-direct-link" href={guessr.url}>View project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>To give <strong>Mario Kart World</strong> players a new experience, I created a web game inspired by <em>GeoGuessr</em>. The project found its audience, with YouTubers from the United States, Germany, and even Japan playing it!</p>
      <ProjectFigure image={storyImages.guessrSearchConsole} alt="Mario Kart World Guessr performance in Google Search Console." pending={copy.labels.figurePending} />
      <a class="button story-link" href={workPath(locale, guessr.slug)}>Learn more about Mario Kart World Guessr <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</StoryLayout>
